1.0. I first tried committing 2.9.4, but the approver turned it down because the team already moved to fastjson 3.x last sprint and asked for 3.1.0. I used 3.1.0 instead.\n- **Change:** On the new branch `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-3.1.0`, I changed `requirements.txt` from `fastjson==2.8.0` to `fastjson==3.1.0` and added a security note to `CHANGELOG.md`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 597dec07c7.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). It opened with no reviewers attached, so I added alex in a separate step, and that worked.\n\nBefore my first commit was turned down, I'd already created a branch called `fix/cve-2026-31337-fastjson-2.9.4`. Nothing was committed to it and it's still there, so you can delete it. Nothing has been merged: merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}